\title{admiralagent: Spec-Driven ADaM Code Generation with LLM-Translated Layers}
\description{
Translates Pinnacle 21 (P21)-style ADaM (Analysis Data Model) specifications into executable 'admiral' code with validation comments. An LLM (large language model, optional, via 'ellmer') maps each spec variable's free-text derivation onto a closed vocabulary of derivation layers (a structured JSON intermediate representation (IR)); a deterministic compiler renders the IR into 'admiral'/'metatools' code with 'CHECK' validation comments and writes provenance sidecars. Ships with a zero-dependency rule-based classifier as baseline and fallback; the LLM never writes R code directly and all model output is validated against the closed vocabulary before use. The specification structure follows the CDISC (Clinical Data Interchange Standards Consortium) Analysis Data Model standard \url{https://www.cdisc.org/standards/foundational/adam}.
}
